  "result": "Excellent! The line discounts feature is fully implemented and tested. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## What Was Implemented\n\n**Line Discount Support** \u2014 Lines can now carry a `discountPercent` (0-100, decimals allowed):\n\n### Key Changes:\n\n1. **`src/errors.js`** \u2014 Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error code\n\n2. **`src/invoices.js`** \u2014 Enhanced with:\n   - **createInvoice**: Accepts optional `discountPercent` in line input, validates it (must be 0-100, must be a number)\n   - **addLine**: Accepts optional `discountPercent`, validates same rules\n   - **lineDiscount()**: New helper that calculates discount as `lineTotal * discountPercent / 100`, uses `roundCents()`, clamps to 0\n   - **invoiceTotals()**: Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }` where:\n     - `discount` = sum of all line discounts\n     - `total` = subtotal - discount (clamped to 0)\n     - All values clamped to 0 minimum (no negatives)\n\n3. **Tests** \u2014 Added 19 comprehensive test cases for:\n   - Discount acceptance and validation\n   - Decimal percentages (12.5%)\n   - Boundary cases (0%, 100%)\n   - Fractional cent rounding\n   - Multiple lines with different discounts\n   - Non-mutation guarantees\n\n**All 79 tests pass** (60 existing + 19 new). The implementation honors all house rules: integer cents throughout, never throws (returns error codes), never mutates arguments, and clamps all amounts to 0 minimum.",
